abstract: >-
  Programs, certificates, run logs and Lean 4 checks for the paper "The Sphere
  Packing Problem in Dimension 4 and the Twenty-Four-Cell Conjecture". The
  paper proves that a Voronoi cell of a packing of unit balls in R^4 has
  volume at least 8, with equality only for the 24-cell of D_4, when at most
  twenty-three or at least thirty-one other centres lie within sqrt 6 of its
  centre, and when no centre lies strictly between 2 + 4e-26 and sqrt 6. It
  reduces the remaining cells to two explicit statements, (G) and (C_M) for 25
  <= M <= 30, which together would give the optimality of D_4 among all
  packings and which remain open. The package contains the verification of the
  certificate of de Laat, Leijenhorst and de Muinck Keizer for twenty-four
  contacts, with its zonal matrices recomputed in exact arithmetic; the three-
  point certificate for twenty-three contacts and its extension to centres at
  any distance below sqrt 6; the rigidity spectrum of the root system and the
  explicit constant of the near-contact theorem; the certificate that no 25
  points of S^3 have pairwise inner products at most 1/2 + 0.008; the two-
  point certificates for thirty-one or more centres and the radial counts for
  twenty-four to thirty; the second-level programme on the enlarged domain;
  and Lean 4 checks of the finite arithmetic of these steps. Part of the code
  was developed with the assistance of Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic.
